  "description": "FILGEO crystallizes in the hexagonal crystal system with space group P -6 2 m. Reported CIF formula moiety: C12 H54 Cr2 N6 O27 Tb3 9+,3(Na1 1+),6(Cl1 O4 1-),6(Cl1 1-),6(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Cr2 (Cr) has 6 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 9 O neighbors; Tb2A (Tb) has 9 O neighbors; Tb2B (Tb) has 9 O neighbors; Cr2C (Cr) has 6 O neighbors; Cr1 (Cr) has 6 O neighbors; Tb1 (Tb) has 9 O neighbors; Tb1A (Tb) has 9 O neighbors; Tb1B (Tb) has 9 O neighbors; Cr1C (Cr) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 18 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.459-4.038 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 102.54-111.98°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula Na3[Tb3Cr2(HGly)6(μ3-OH)6(H2O)9]·(ClO4)6·Cl6·6H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 9 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
